  "summary": "Reconciled all five St. Brigid discharges per RBC-TOC-02. Each patient has a progress note; four also have a §8 addendum.\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005): furosemide changed to 40 mg BID per the signed addendum (mr-t0001). KCl stopped. Pantoprazole was a formulary substitution, so not ordered and omeprazole kept. Lisinopril was first kept on hold (K 5.4 on 10/21), then resumed after the 10/23 repeat BMP (K 4.7, Cr 1.21). Messaged PCP: an unsigned draft addendum proposes furosemide 60 mg BID (not acted on), and old task task-t0003 is moot and could not be cancelled from my queue.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004): carvedilol was raised to 12.5 mg BID per the summary, then a signed addendum arrived and it was corrected back to 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0016). Flagged to PCP: atorvastatin fills cover only ~24% of the 180 days before admission (no change made), and glipizide from an outside endocrinologist is not addressed at discharge.\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044): lisinopril was resumed on the 10/22 BMP (Cr 1.08, K 4.6), then re-held when K 5.5 on 10/23 arrived. PCP task due 10/26.\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069): lisinopril was resumed on the 10/21 labs (Cr 1.12, K 4.4), then re-held when K 5.4 (collected 10/22) arrived. PCP task due 10/26.\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067): metformin kept on hold because the only creatinine was drawn in hospital, not after discharge. PCP task due 10/24, when the post-discharge BMP is expected. No other changes.\n\nAll arrival inbox items were reviewed and closed.",
